hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"436","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a slave girl menstruates, it is not proper for anything of her to be seen except her face and her hands up to the joint."
"437","'Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu 'Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anything of the two sandals protrude over the feet."
"438","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I came to Madinah and was brought two sandals which they claimed were the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with two straps, the ends of their thongs folded into their knots. I mentioned it to Muhammad, so he sent for his sandals on the spot and altered them."
"439","'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I saw the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two front straps."
"440","It was read to al-Harith ibn Miskin while I was present: Ibn al-Qasim informed you, from Malik — and he was asked about the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whether he had seen it: how was its shape? He said: It was toward roundness, its middle narrowed at its rear, narrowed and heeled at its back. I said: Did it have two straps? He said: That is what I believe, with the family of Rabi'ah al-Makhzumi from their mother Umm Kulthum."
"441","Ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: I came to a shoemaker in Madinah and ordered him to make my sandals with two front straps. He said to me: Shall I not make them as I saw the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: With whom did you see them? He said: With Fatimah bint 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abbas. I said: Then make them so. He made both of them on the right pattern."
"442","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Yazid al-Haddadi Abu Hashim narrated to me: Abu 'Abd al-Da'im narrated to me, from Abu Malih, that the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, or the strap of his sandal, so he walked in one sandal until he repaired the other."
